From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 11:36:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] arm64: dts: qcom: kaanapali-oneplus-iceland: WAKE# back
 on the Wi-Fi root port

Wake-on-WLAN needs the WCN7860's WAKE# (GPIO 104, PDC pin 148): with
the chip armed for WoW and kept in D0, the firmware asserts it when a
magic packet or pattern arrives, and the PCI core's dedicated wake IRQ
on the root port wakes the system from s2idle.

The PCI core makes the root port a wakeup source with this GPIO. The
device package keeps the root port's wakeup off unless Wake-on-WLAN is
enabled (as before 26b905ebedae, which dropped the GPIO because no
Wake-on-WLAN was set up); with Wake-on-WLAN off, ath12k still powers the
chip off for a suspend.

Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts | 8 +++++---
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts
index 586fee50b..d11551573 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts
@@ -1715,10 +1715,12 @@ &pcie0_phy {
 
 &pcie_port0 {
 	/*
-	 * No wake-gpios: the Wi-Fi chip's WAKE# (GPIO 104) would make the
-	 * root port a wakeup source, and Wake-on-WLAN is not set up (Wi-Fi
-	 * is powered off for a suspend).
+	 * The Wi-Fi chip's WAKE# (GPIO 104, PDC pin 148), for Wake-on-WLAN.
+	 * The PCI core makes the root port a wakeup source with it; the
+	 * device package keeps that off unless Wake-on-WLAN is enabled (with
+	 * Wake-on-WLAN off, Wi-Fi is powered off for a suspend).
 	 */
+	wake-gpios = <&tlmm 104 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
 	reset-gpios = <&tlmm 102 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
 
 	wifi@0 {
